# {{.SudoersFile}}: what a brokered command may sudo to.
#
# Written by `faramir init --allow-sudo` and REWRITTEN BY EVERY RUN. Re-running
# init without --allow-sudo removes this file: the grant is the one place the
# executor's reach grows, so taking it away is a re-run rather than an edit.
#
# {{.ExecUser}} is the uid every brokered command runs as. It gets full sudo
# and an authentication step it cannot satisfy by itself: pam_service below
# points sudo at {{.PamFile}}, whose auth step asks the broker whether a human
# approved the command making the call. No password exists to be typed,
# stored or stolen.
#
# NOT NOPASSWD, and that is the whole design. NOPASSWD skips PAM entirely, so
# the question would never be asked and anything running as this uid would be
# root for the asking. The PASSWD tag is what makes sudo authenticate, and
# authenticating is what reaches the broker.
#
# pam_service is what keeps a mistake here from reaching anybody else: every
# other account's sudo reads the stock /etc/pam.d/sudo, which faramir never
# touches.
#
# timestamp_timeout=0 turns off sudo's credential cache, leaving the broker to
# decide what an approval covers. It scopes one to the brokered command the
# human was shown: every `sudo` that one run makes, and nothing after it ends.
# sudo's timestamp would instead scope it to the next fifteen minutes, which
# anything starting a command inside that window could ride.
#
# env_file is the other half of env_reset. sudo discards the caller's
# environment, which is right -- the executor's uid is shared by every brokered
# command, so anything it carries is a value one of them chose. What a brokered
# command should have instead comes from a file this policy names, which that uid
# cannot write. Not env_keep, which would preserve the caller's own value under
# the same name and hand root exactly what the reset threw away.
Defaults:{{.ExecUser}} pam_service={{.PamService}}
Defaults:{{.ExecUser}} timestamp_timeout=0
Defaults:{{.ExecUser}} passwd_tries=1
Defaults:{{.ExecUser}} env_file={{.SudoEnvFile}}
{{.ExecUser}} ALL=(ALL:ALL) PASSWD: ALL
